@startuml
title OneDrive Client for Linux - Main Synchronisation Activity
start

:Initialise configuration, logging, database,\nMicrosoft API and runtime services;
:Validate authentication / token state;
:Validate service reachability and system time when enabled;
note right
  This diagram shows high-level orchestration.
  Data-preservation decisions are made by the
  lower-level conflict and transactional transfer
  paths shown in the following diagrams.
end note

if (~--local-first?) then (yes)
  :Database consistency / known local state pass;
  note right
    Local filesystem intent is evaluated first.
    ~--local-first changes ordering, not the
    requirement to protect independent online data.
  end note
  :Apply locally modified / deleted tracked items;
  :Scan local filesystem for new data;
  :Upload eligible new local items;
  :Enumerate online state (/delta or generated response);
  :Process online JSON and apply remaining remote changes;
else (no)
  :Enumerate online state (/delta or generated response);
  :Validate, filter and classify online JSON;
  :Process root and deletion state;
  note right
    An online deletion of a tracked file that has
    independently changed locally is a data-loss
    prevention case: the local content is preserved
    before the online deletion is honoured.
  end note
  :Route known items to applyPotentiallyChangedItem();
  :Route untracked online items to applyPotentiallyNewLocalItem();
  :Process queued downloads transactionally;
  note right
    File replacement is staged to .partial first.
    The canonical local path is only replaced after
    validation and any required safeBackup succeeds.
  end note

  :Database consistency / known local state pass;
  :Apply locally modified / deleted tracked items;

  if (~--download-only?) then (yes)
    :Skip new-local-data upload scan;
  else (no)
    :Scan local filesystem for new data;
    :Apply local client-side filtering;
    :Create directories / upload files as required;

    if (force_children_scan enabled?) then (yes)
      :No duplicate final online traversal;
    else (no)
      :Perform final online true-up;
      :Process any additional remote changes;
    endif
  endif
endif

:In monitor mode, reconcile expected/client-generated\nfilesystem effects at the applicable phase boundaries;
:Report transfer / synchronisation failures;
stop
@enduml
